1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,702
There are two words that Muslims say thousands of times throughout

2
00:00:04,702 --> 00:00:06,024
their lives.

3
00:00:06,049 --> 00:00:07,187
Before eating.

4
00:00:07,187 --> 00:00:08,649
Before drinking.

5
00:00:08,649 --> 00:00:11,155
Before starting something important.

6
00:00:11,459 --> 00:00:15,290
But have you ever stopped and thought about what actually happens

7
00:00:15,290 --> 00:00:16,751
when you say them?

8
00:00:17,055 --> 00:00:18,284
Bismillah.

9
00:00:18,367 --> 00:00:20,257
In the name of Allah.

10
00:00:20,468 --> 00:00:25,540
These words are short, but they carry an incredibly powerful reminder.

11
00:00:25,681 --> 00:00:29,280
The Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him,

12
00:00:29,280 --> 00:00:34,180
taught his companions to remember Allah in their everyday actions.

13
00:00:34,180 --> 00:00:39,578
And in authentic narrations, he explained something fascinating about what happens

14
00:00:39,578 --> 00:00:43,735
when a person remembers Allah before entering their home and before

15
00:00:43,735 --> 00:00:44,720
eating.

16
00:00:44,745 --> 00:00:47,715
But what happens when someone forgets?

17
00:00:47,856 --> 00:00:51,850
Why did the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him,

18
00:00:51,850 --> 00:00:54,729
teach us to say Bismillah before eating?

19
00:00:54,729 --> 00:00:57,969
And how can these two simple words become part of our

20
00:00:57,969 --> 00:01:00,161
daily protection and worship?

21
00:01:00,558 --> 00:01:05,118
Let's explore what the Quran and authentic Sunnah teach us.

22
00:01:05,631 --> 00:01:06,953
Chapter one.

23
00:01:07,466 --> 00:01:10,204
What does Bismillah actually mean?

24
00:01:10,334 --> 00:01:12,898
The word Bismillah means:

25
00:01:12,911 --> 00:01:14,755
"In the name of Allah."

26
00:01:15,245 --> 00:01:19,910
But saying Bismillah is more than simply repeating a phrase.

27
00:01:19,982 --> 00:01:23,407
It is a reminder that everything we do should begin with

28
00:01:23,407 --> 00:01:25,541
remembering our Creator.

29
00:01:25,740 --> 00:01:28,745
When you say Bismillah before eating,

30
00:01:28,770 --> 00:01:31,603
you're acknowledging that the food in front of you is a

31
00:01:31,603 --> 00:01:33,284
blessing from Allah.

32
00:01:33,368 --> 00:01:36,607
When you say Bismillah before beginning your work,

33
00:01:36,607 --> 00:01:41,738
you're reminding yourself that your abilities and opportunities ultimately come from

34
00:01:41,738 --> 00:01:42,502
Him.

35
00:01:42,713 --> 00:01:46,786
And when you say Bismillah before starting something important,

36
00:01:46,811 --> 00:01:50,548
you're acknowledging that you need Allah's help and blessing.

37
00:01:50,759 --> 00:01:54,101
Think about how often we rush through our days.

38
00:01:54,126 --> 00:01:55,101
We wake up.

39
00:01:55,101 --> 00:01:55,960
We eat.

40
00:01:55,960 --> 00:01:56,750
We work.

41
00:01:56,750 --> 00:01:57,830
We drive.

42
00:01:57,830 --> 00:02:00,314
We spend time with our families.

43
00:02:00,314 --> 00:02:04,238
Sometimes we become so busy that we forget to remember the

44
00:02:04,238 --> 00:02:08,103
One who gave us the ability to do all these things.

45
00:02:08,615 --> 00:02:12,830
Bismillah brings that reminder back into our everyday lives.

46
00:02:12,830 --> 00:02:16,208
It reminds us that we are not independent of Allah.

47
00:02:16,208 --> 00:02:18,147
We need Him in everything.

48
00:02:18,147 --> 00:02:19,399
Chapter two.

49
00:02:19,912 --> 00:02:23,556
What happens when you say Bismillah before eating?

50
00:02:23,766 --> 00:02:27,447
One of the most important times to say Bismillah is before

51
00:02:27,447 --> 00:02:28,190
eating.

52
00:02:28,190 --> 00:02:31,836
The Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him,

53
00:02:31,836 --> 00:02:35,981
taught Umar ibn Abi Salamah, a young boy who was eating

54
00:02:35,981 --> 00:02:36,712
with him:

55
00:02:36,712 --> 00:02:39,556
"Young boy, mention the name of Allah,

56
00:02:39,556 --> 00:02:42,714
eat with your right hand, and eat from what is nearest

57
00:02:42,714 --> 00:02:43,653
to you."

58
00:02:43,678 --> 00:02:48,877
This narration is recorded in Sahih al-Bukhari and Sahih Muslim.

59
00:02:48,903 --> 00:02:51,759
Notice how simple the instructions are.

60
00:02:51,759 --> 00:02:53,024
Remember Allah.

61
00:02:53,024 --> 00:02:54,719
Use your right hand.

62
00:02:54,719 --> 00:02:57,041
Eat from what is closest to you.

63
00:02:57,041 --> 00:03:00,373
These are everyday actions, but the Prophet,

64
00:03:00,373 --> 00:03:02,545
peace and blessings be upon him,

65
00:03:02,545 --> 00:03:06,620
taught us that even eating should have manners and remembrance of

66
00:03:06,620 --> 00:03:07,593
Allah.

67
00:03:08,106 --> 00:03:10,949
But there is another fascinating narration.

68
00:03:11,159 --> 00:03:15,743
In Sahih Muslim, the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him,

69
00:03:15,769 --> 00:03:20,354
explained that when someone enters their home and remembers Allah,

70
00:03:20,354 --> 00:03:24,720
and remembers Allah when eating, Shaytan says that there is no

71
00:03:24,720 --> 00:03:28,213
place to spend the night and no evening meal for them.

72
00:03:28,423 --> 00:03:33,009
But when a person enters without remembering Allah and eats without

73
00:03:33,009 --> 00:03:37,943
mentioning His name, Shaytan says that he and his followers have

74
00:03:37,943 --> 00:03:40,821
found a place to stay and food to eat.

75
00:03:40,962 --> 00:03:42,330
Think about that.

76
00:03:42,355 --> 00:03:47,115
Something as simple as remembering Allah when entering your home and

77
00:03:47,115 --> 00:03:51,153
before eating has significance beyond what we can see.

78
00:03:51,295 --> 00:03:54,963
It is a reminder that our homes should be places where

79
00:03:54,963 --> 00:03:56,866
Allah is remembered.

80
00:03:57,169 --> 00:04:01,254
And our meals should begin with gratitude to Him.

81
00:04:01,767 --> 00:04:02,951
Chapter three.

82
00:04:02,951 --> 00:04:05,376
What if you forget to say Bismillah?

83
00:04:05,888 --> 00:04:08,083
Now, let's say you're hungry.

84
00:04:08,083 --> 00:04:09,163
You sit down.

85
00:04:09,163 --> 00:04:10,484
You start eating.

86
00:04:10,498 --> 00:04:13,157
And suddenly, halfway through your meal,

87
00:04:13,157 --> 00:04:14,596
you remember something.

88
00:04:14,596 --> 00:04:16,558
You forgot to say Bismillah.

89
00:04:16,558 --> 00:04:17,777
What should you do?

90
00:04:17,777 --> 00:04:20,854
The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him,

91
00:04:20,854 --> 00:04:23,083
taught us exactly what to say.

92
00:04:23,083 --> 00:04:27,623
In a narration recorded in Sunan Abi Dawud and Jami at-Tirmidhi,

93
00:04:27,623 --> 00:04:30,616
the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him,

94
00:04:30,641 --> 00:04:34,461
explained that if someone forgets to mention Allah at the beginning

95
00:04:34,461 --> 00:04:36,760
of their meal, they should say:

96
00:04:36,760 --> 00:04:40,426
"Bismillahi awwalahu wa akhirahu."

97
00:04:40,509 --> 00:04:41,322
Meaning:

98
00:04:41,322 --> 00:04:45,513
"In the name of Allah, at its beginning and its end."

99
00:04:45,513 --> 00:04:47,148
Isn't that beautiful?

100
00:04:47,232 --> 00:04:51,318
Even when you forget, Islam gives you a way to remember

101
00:04:51,318 --> 00:04:53,605
Allah and correct yourself.

102
00:04:53,605 --> 00:04:55,184
You don't have to give up.

103
00:04:55,184 --> 00:04:58,366
You don't have to feel like the opportunity has passed.

104
00:04:58,366 --> 00:05:01,173
Just remember Allah and continue.

105
00:05:01,686 --> 00:05:04,738
This is one of the beautiful things about Islam.

106
00:05:04,821 --> 00:05:07,224
It teaches us to remember Allah,

107
00:05:07,224 --> 00:05:09,823
even when we make small mistakes.

108
00:05:10,335 --> 00:05:11,646
Chapter four.

109
00:05:12,042 --> 00:05:15,453
Saying Bismillah when entering your home.

110
00:05:15,850 --> 00:05:18,950
Now, here's something many Muslims may overlook.

111
00:05:18,950 --> 00:05:22,501
Saying Bismillah is not only connected to food.

112
00:05:22,712 --> 00:05:26,624
Remembering Allah when entering your home is also part of the

113
00:05:26,624 --> 00:05:27,574
Sunnah.

114
00:05:28,226 --> 00:05:31,140
The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him,

115
00:05:31,140 --> 00:05:35,889
explained that when someone enters their house and mentions Allah's name,

116
00:05:35,889 --> 00:05:39,651
Shaytan tells his followers that they have no place to spend

117
00:05:39,651 --> 00:05:40,719
the night there.

118
00:05:40,719 --> 00:05:43,668
This narration is found in Sahih Muslim.

119
00:05:43,668 --> 00:05:46,745
Imagine coming home after a long day.

120
00:05:46,745 --> 00:05:48,115
You open the door.

121
00:05:48,115 --> 00:05:49,810
You enter your house.

122
00:05:49,810 --> 00:05:53,386
Instead of immediately becoming distracted by your phone,

123
00:05:53,386 --> 00:05:56,124
television, or everything waiting for you,

124
00:05:56,149 --> 00:05:57,890
remember Allah.

125
00:05:57,890 --> 00:05:59,295
Say Bismillah.

126
00:05:59,295 --> 00:06:01,547
Give salam to your family.

127
00:06:01,547 --> 00:06:05,332
Make your home a place where Allah is remembered.

128
00:06:05,332 --> 00:06:08,653
Because a Muslim's home should not only be a place to

129
00:06:08,653 --> 00:06:09,419
sleep.

130
00:06:09,419 --> 00:06:11,393
It should be a place of prayer,

131
00:06:11,393 --> 00:06:14,690
remembrance, kindness, and worship.

132
00:06:14,690 --> 00:06:16,081
Chapter five.

133
00:06:16,106 --> 00:06:19,624
The blessing of remembering Allah in private.

134
00:06:19,624 --> 00:06:24,593
Something important to understand is that remembering Allah is not only

135
00:06:24,593 --> 00:06:27,506
for moments when other people can hear you.

136
00:06:27,716 --> 00:06:31,244
You can remember Allah when nobody is watching.

137
00:06:31,327 --> 00:06:35,029
You can say Bismillah before eating alone.

138
00:06:35,240 --> 00:06:38,874
You can remember Allah before beginning your work.

139
00:06:38,874 --> 00:06:41,939
You can make dua before leaving your home.

140
00:06:41,939 --> 00:06:45,468
And you can thank Allah for blessings that nobody else even

141
00:06:45,468 --> 00:06:46,662
knows about.

142
00:06:46,745 --> 00:06:50,936
Islam teaches us that our relationship with Allah is not limited

143
00:06:50,936 --> 00:06:52,062
to the mosque.

144
00:06:52,062 --> 00:06:54,489
It is part of our entire lives.

145
00:06:54,489 --> 00:06:58,146
You don't need to be standing in prayer to remember Allah.

146
00:06:58,146 --> 00:07:01,246
You don't need to be surrounded by other Muslims.

147
00:07:01,246 --> 00:07:04,264
You can remember Him wherever you are.

148
00:07:04,264 --> 00:07:08,467
And that is one of the beautiful lessons behind saying Bismillah.

149
00:07:08,467 --> 00:07:13,876
It turns ordinary moments into opportunities to remember your Creator.

150
00:07:14,388 --> 00:07:15,666
Chapter six.

151
00:07:15,666 --> 00:07:18,880
Don't turn Bismillah into just a habit.

152
00:07:18,905 --> 00:07:21,503
But there is something we should reflect on.

153
00:07:21,529 --> 00:07:25,581
Sometimes we repeat words so often that we stop thinking about

154
00:07:25,581 --> 00:07:26,717
their meaning.

155
00:07:26,928 --> 00:07:31,421
We say Bismillah before eating, but our minds are already somewhere

156
00:07:31,421 --> 00:07:32,266
else.

157
00:07:32,477 --> 00:07:37,723
We say Alhamdulillah without truly thinking about the blessings we have.

158
00:07:37,864 --> 00:07:42,320
We make dua, but sometimes our hearts are distracted.

159
00:07:42,624 --> 00:07:45,631
The goal isn't simply to repeat words.

160
00:07:45,631 --> 00:07:49,518
The goal is to remember Allah with sincerity.

161
00:07:49,543 --> 00:07:53,108
When you say Bismillah, remember who Allah is.

162
00:07:53,108 --> 00:07:55,915
Remember that your food comes from Him.

163
00:07:55,941 --> 00:07:58,899
Remember that your strength comes from Him.

164
00:07:59,040 --> 00:08:03,417
Remember that every opportunity you have is ultimately a blessing from

165
00:08:03,417 --> 00:08:04,158
Him.

166
00:08:04,184 --> 00:08:07,980
And remember that even the smallest everyday action can become an

167
00:08:07,980 --> 00:08:11,486
act of worship when it is done with the right intention

168
00:08:11,486 --> 00:08:14,549
and in a way that pleases Allah.

169
00:08:15,550 --> 00:08:16,802
Chapter seven.

170
00:08:17,198 --> 00:08:19,994
Make these words part of your daily life.

171
00:08:20,577 --> 00:08:23,408
So how can you bring this into your routine?

172
00:08:23,862 --> 00:08:25,672
Start with something simple.

173
00:08:25,732 --> 00:08:27,692
Before eating, say Bismillah.

174
00:08:27,949 --> 00:08:30,712
When entering your home, remember Allah.

175
00:08:30,712 --> 00:08:32,997
When you forget, don't give up.

176
00:08:33,104 --> 00:08:35,876
Remember Allah as soon as you recall.

177
00:08:35,960 --> 00:08:39,222
Teach your children to say Bismillah before eating.

178
00:08:39,222 --> 00:08:41,265
Remind your family gently.

179
00:08:41,265 --> 00:08:45,491
And most importantly, don't allow these words to become something you

180
00:08:45,491 --> 00:08:47,904
say without understanding.

181
00:08:47,987 --> 00:08:51,656
Because remembering Allah should be part of your everyday life.

182
00:08:51,656 --> 00:08:53,281
Not just during Ramadan.

183
00:08:53,281 --> 00:08:55,278
Not just during difficult times.

184
00:08:55,278 --> 00:08:57,345
And not just when you need something.

185
00:08:57,345 --> 00:08:59,969
Remember Allah when life is going well.

186
00:08:59,969 --> 00:09:02,755
Remember Allah when life becomes difficult.

187
00:09:02,755 --> 00:09:06,958
And remember Him during the ordinary moments that you might otherwise

188
00:09:06,958 --> 00:09:08,337
take for granted.

189
00:09:08,478 --> 00:09:10,777
The next time you sit down to eat,

190
00:09:10,777 --> 00:09:12,482
remember these words.

191
00:09:12,786 --> 00:09:13,898
Bismillah.

192
00:09:14,550 --> 00:09:17,277
The next time you walk through your front door,

193
00:09:17,360 --> 00:09:19,030
remember Allah.

194
00:09:19,427 --> 00:09:22,364
And the next time you begin something important,

195
00:09:22,364 --> 00:09:25,638
remember that you are a servant of the One who created

196
00:09:25,638 --> 00:09:26,344
you.

197
00:09:26,427 --> 00:09:28,123
Two simple words.

198
00:09:28,123 --> 00:09:31,975
But a powerful reminder of who we belong to.

199
00:09:32,279 --> 00:09:36,377
May Allah make us among those who remember Him frequently,

200
00:09:36,377 --> 00:09:39,071
bless our homes, accept our deeds,

201
00:09:39,071 --> 00:09:41,368
and protect us from Shaytan.

202
00:09:41,393 --> 00:09:45,085
May Allah allow us to live our lives with sincerity and

203
00:09:45,085 --> 00:09:46,141
gratitude.

204
00:09:46,141 --> 00:09:47,070
Ameen.

205
00:09:47,070 --> 00:09:48,997
And Allah knows best.
